<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # The Vessels Are Big Because... – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Visiting the Panama Canal</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> The Vessels Are Big Because...</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Extract specific information from announcements or instructions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can extract specific information from talks about the Panama Canal (e.g., 'What does the Panama Canal connect?' 'The Panama Canal connects the Atlantic Ocean to the Pacific Ocean.'). Can follow simple, oral, multi-step directions related to an oral description of a visit to the Panama Canal (e.g., 'Draw the canal and color it blue, and then label the two oceans.' 'Color the largest vessel red, and then draw small waves.'). Can get the main points of a simple talk about the Panama Canal ('Private boats can go through the canal.').</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 40%; text-align: left;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 45%; text-align: left;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 15%; text-align: left;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5px;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows a large picture of the Panama Canal with different vessels, including ships, boats, and yachts. The teacher points to different parts of the picture and asks students simple questions like "What do you see?" and "Is it big or small?". The teacher introduces key vocabulary orally: 'canal,' 'vessel,' 'ship,' 'boat,' 'yacht,' 'ocean,' 'connect,' 'big,' 'small,' 'travel,' 'see.' Students listen and point to the corresponding objects in the picture.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher holds up flashcards for 'canal,' 'vessel,' 'ship,' 'boat,' 'ocean,' 'big,' 'small.' For each flashcard, the teacher clearly pronounces the word and models its sound, emphasizing the /k/ sound in 'canal' and the /b/ sound in 'boat.' The teacher says, "This is a big ship. This is a small boat. The canal connects the oceans." Students listen and repeat chorally. The teacher demonstrates simple actions for 'travel' (moving hands) and 'connect' (bringing hands together).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of the new vocabulary through simple questions.
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is a yacht a big boat or a small boat?" (Expected answer: "A small boat.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Does the canal connect the land or the oceans?" (Expected answer: "The oceans.")</li>
                    The teacher provides examples like, "Look! This vessel is bigger than that yacht," and encourages students to listen for the comparison.
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5-7 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5px;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Visiting the Panama Canal")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, simple audio recording (e.g., 60-90 seconds) of an announcement or a guide describing the Panama Canal from a visitor's perspective. The language will be clear, slow, and use the target vocabulary and grammar. (e.g., "Welcome to the Panama Canal! We are at Miraflores Locks. Look! A big vessel is traveling through the canal now. It connects the Atlantic Ocean and the Pacific Ocean. That ship is bigger than the small yacht. Many people are observing the vessels. It is a fascinating and historic place.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Extract specific information from announcements or instructions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question (first listen):</b> "What is the recording about? Is it about food or the Panama Canal?" (Students listen and choose).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (second listen):</b> The teacher gives sentences, and students listen to the audio again and say "True" or "False" with thumbs up/down.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The recording says a small boat is traveling through the canal." (False - it says a big vessel)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The canal connects two oceans." (True)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Many people are watching the vessels." (True)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching (third listen):</b> The teacher provides two options for students to choose from after listening for specific details.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What place are they visiting? (a) Miraflores Locks (b) The beach."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is traveling through the canal now? (a) a big vessel (b) a small car."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(10-12 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5px;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Listening)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice listening for specific vocabulary (canal, boat, ocean, vessel, ship, yacht, big, small, connect, travel, observe) and simple sentences using Present simple ("The Panama Canal connects two oceans.") and Present continuous ("A big vessel is crossing the canal now.") and basic comparatives ("That ship is bigger than this yacht.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listen and Draw/Label (Controlled Practice):</b> The teacher gives each student a simple worksheet with an outline of a canal and some blank spaces for vessels and oceans. The teacher reads out simple instructions one by one. Students listen and follow the directions.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Listen and draw a big vessel in the canal. Color it red."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Draw a small boat next to the vessel. Color it blue."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Label the 'Atlantic Ocean' on one side and the 'Pacific Ocean' on the other side of the canal."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Teacher models pronunciation of /k/ in 'canal' and /b/ in 'boat' clearly during instructions. Teacher also practices blending: /b/ /oʊt/ 'boat' by saying sounds and having students blend).</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listen and Choose (Semi-controlled):</b> The teacher plays 3-4 short audio descriptions of vessels at the canal. For each description, students listen and circle the correct image from two options (e.g., "This is the biggest ship." vs. "This is a small yacht."). The options could also include comparative statements (e.g., "The blue ship is bigger than the yellow boat."). The teacher emphasizes attentive listening for key adjectives.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listen and Compare (Pair Check):</b> In pairs, students receive a simple "spot the difference" picture of the Panama Canal with vessels. The teacher reads a short audio description of *one* of the pictures. Students listen carefully and then, in pairs, discuss which picture the teacher described (Picture A or Picture B) and identify 1-2 differences, reinforcing language like "Picture A has a big vessel, but Picture B has a small boat" (comparing things). This encourages respectful conversations as they share opinions: "I think it's Picture A. What do you think?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(12-15 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5px;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Visiting the Panama Canal")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative "Follow the Guide's Directions" activity. Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group receives a large blank poster paper and markers. The teacher acts as a "Panama Canal Guide" and gives a sequence of multi-step oral instructions related to drawing a scene at the Canal, using all target vocabulary and grammar.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher starts: "Hello, visitors! Welcome to the Panama Canal. Today, we are going to draw what we see and hear. Listen carefully to my directions."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher gives 3-4 sentences of instructions at a time, allowing groups to listen and execute. Example instructions:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"First, draw the big canal. Make it wide and deep. Color the water blue." (Describing facts, following directions)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Next, draw two oceans, the Atlantic Ocean and the Pacific Ocean. Label them on your drawing." (Describing facts, specific information)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Now, draw three vessels. Draw the biggest ship first, then a smaller vessel, and then the smallest yacht. Color the biggest ship red." (Comparatives and superlatives, following directions)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Many people are watching. Draw some people observing the vessels. What do you think? Do you like the canal? Why?" (Describing current events, sociolinguistics: inviting participation)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students listen to the teacher's instructions, clarify with group members (silently or with pointing), and draw on their poster. The teacher circulates, observing listening comprehension and group collaboration.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency of understanding oral instructions, collaborative interaction, and successful completion of the multi-step drawing task based on listening.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(10-12 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5px;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during Stage 4 and a quick comprehension check at the end.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The teacher plays a final short audio clip (20-30 seconds) describing one specific vessel or event at the canal. Students listen and then point to the corresponding part of their group's drawing or a flashcard, or answer a simple Yes/No question related to what they heard.</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Audio example: "Listen! A big blue vessel is crossing the canal now. It is transporting many goods."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher question: "Is the vessel red?" (Students say "No") "Is it big?" (Students say "Yes")</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can the student point to the correct object/picture after listening to instructions? (Extract specific information)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can the student follow multi-step oral directions?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Does the student demonstrate understanding of the target vocabulary (vessel, boat, canal, ocean, big, small)?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Does the student engage respectfully in group activity?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer two quick questions orally or by showing thumbs up/down as they leave the class:
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did you understand the guide's directions today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can you tell me one new word you heard today?" (e.g., 'vessel,' 'canal')</li>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5-7 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5px;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy to understand today when listening about the Panama Canal?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was a little difficult to understand, and why?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students extract specific information from oral input? The visual aids and multi-step directions in the practice stage seemed particularly effective.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for the next listening lesson? Some students struggled with differentiating between 'vessel' and 'ship'; more targeted practice for these specific words might be needed. Perhaps more varied accents in audio recordings could be introduced gradually.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Were the instructions clear enough for a 4th-grade A1.2 level? Yes, but I need to monitor the length of sentences more closely.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> The vocabulary introduced and listened to today (canal, vessel, ship, ocean, connect, big, small) will be reviewed and then applied to a short written text about the Panama Canal in Lesson 2, focusing on reading comprehension of the same content.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(3-5 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>